  "rationale": "Genome-wide knockout library (about 4 guides per gene, 1,000 non-targeting) in HT29 cells carrying an endogenous XBP1s-GFP reporter, treated with tunicamycin (Tm) or DMSO and FACS-sorted into GFP-high and GFP-low bins in three replicates (You et al. 2021). GEO deposits everything under one GSM; column names give treatment, bin and replicate, and the sample index file lists replicates A-C. Replicate libraries correlate most strongly with the same replicate in the other bin and treatment (Spearman 0.57-0.64 vs about 0.45), so high and low bins of a replicate come from the same edited pool and replicate is paired in the model (~ rep + sort). The main contrast is GFP-high vs GFP-low under tunicamycin, the authors' Tm_H-Tm_L MAGeCK-MLE comparison deposited alongside the counts.",
